      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(sessions): reject non-canonical raw transcript cursors",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where raw transcript pagination accepted non-canonical variants of OpenClaw-issued continuation cursors. Appended junk, base64url padding, and extra JSON fields could all resume from the same SQLite transcript position as the canonical cursor.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nRaw transcript cursors now require both their base64url bytes and their complete decoded envelope to round-trip exactly to OpenClaw's encoder output. Pagination queries, cursor fields, reset reasons, and the SQLite schema are unchanged. The compatibility risk is that aliases previously accepted as continuation hints now reset; the production-path proof covers canonical continuation and each malformed alias.\n\n## User Impact\n\nMalformed or structurally altered raw transcript cursors now return the existing `invalid_cursor` reset instead of silently continuing from an equivalent position. Canonical cursors emitted by OpenClaw continue to page normally.\n\n## Evidence\n\nOn Node v24.18.0, I drove the real `readSessionTranscriptRawDelta()` SDK runtime against a real temporary SQLite transcript store. The same harness inserted transcript events, read the first page, then supplied its canonical cursor and three altered variants. `OPENCLAW_STATE_DIR` was isolated to a temporary proof directory.\n\nBefore, using the unmodified `upstream/main` production file, every cursor variant continued as a page:\n\n```text\nBEFORE canonical: page\nBEFORE appendedJunk: page\nBEFORE padding: page\nBEFORE extraField: page\n```\n\nAfter the fix, canonical continuation still works while all non-canonical variants take the existing reset path:\n\n```text\nAFTER canonical: page\nAFTER appendedJunk: reset invalid_cursor\nAFTER padding: reset invalid_cursor\nAFTER extraField: reset invalid_cursor\n```\n\nThe focused SDK regression passes and retains the existing two-page continuation coverage:\n\n```text\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/plugin-sdk/session-transcript-runtime.test.ts\nTest Files  1 passed (1)\nTests       20 passed (20)\n```\n\nAlso run: targeted `oxfmt`, `git diff --check`, and Codex autoreview (`patch is correct`, confidence 0.97, no actionable findings). No live agent turn was run; the affected behavior is fully exercised through the production SDK runtime and SQLite store without substituting the cursor parser or database path.\n\nAI-assisted: Codex helped implement and review the change; the production-path proof and focused test were run manually.\n",
